</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L479" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In addition to these second order equations, there is an important first order equation that appears often in the numerical analysis literature: the advection equation.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L473" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">advection := diff(u(t, x), t)+c*diff(u(t, x), x) = 0;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSphZHZlY3Rpb25HRigvLCYtSSVkaWZmR0YmNiQtSSJ1R0YoNiRJInRHRihJInhHRihGNiIiIiomSSJjR0YoRjgtRjE2JEYzRjdGOEY4IiIhNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L499" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Maple can solve each of the above analytically using <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">pdsolve</Font><Font style="Text">.</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L495" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">parabolic_sol := pdsolve(parabolic);
hyperbolic_sol := pdsolve(hyperbolic);
elliptic_sol := pdsolve(elliptic);
advection_sol := pdsolve(advection);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SS9oeXBlcmJvbGljX3NvbEdGKC8tSSJ1R0YoNiRJInRHRihJInhHRigsJi1JJWZfXzFHRig2IywmKiZJImNHRigiIiJGMkY7ISIiRjNGPEY7LUklZl9fMkdGKDYjLCZGOUY8RjNGO0Y7NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SS1lbGxpcHRpY19zb2xHRigvLUkidUdGKDYkSSJ4R0YoSSJ5R0YoLCYtSSVmX18xR0YoNiMsJkYzIiIiKiZeIyEiIkY5RjJGOUY5RjktSSVmX18yR0YoNiMsJkYzRjkqJl4jRjlGOUYyRjlGOUY5NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SS5hZHZlY3Rpb25fc29sR0YoLy1JInVHRig2JEkidEdGKEkieEdGKC1JJWZfXzFHRig2IywmKiZJImNHRigiIiJGMkY6ISIiRjNGOjcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L477" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">In the last three cases, Maple succeeds in obtaining the general solution to the PDE in terms of <Font style="Text">arbitrary</Font> functions <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiZkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1GIzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiMUYnL0Y2USdub3JtYWxGJ0YyRjUvJS9zdWJzY3JpcHRzaGlmdEdRIjBGJy1GLzYjUSFGJ0Y+">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiZkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1GIzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JFEiMUYnL0Y2USdub3JtYWxGJ0YyRjUvJS9zdWJzY3JpcHRzaGlmdEdRIjBGJy1GLzYjUSFGJ0Y+</Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. In the first case, it succeeds in performing a separation of variables and reducing the problem to a pair of ODEs involving a separation constant <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEjX2NGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRictRiM2JS1JI21uR0YkNiRRIjFGJy9GNlEnbm9ybWFsRidGMkY1LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGPg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEjX2NGJy8lJ2l0YWxpY0dRJXRydWVGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRictRiM2JS1JI21uR0YkNiRRIjFGJy9GNlEnbm9ybWFsRidGMkY1LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGPg==</Equation> (which we relabel as <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>). We can get it to solve these by using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">build</Font> command.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L475" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">parabolic_sol := subs(_c[1] = k, u(t, x) = U(t, x, k), simplify(build(parabolic_sol))) assuming(k&gt;0);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L476" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">However, this is not the general solution to the PDE, which is given by a superposition of these solutions with different choices of <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> as follows.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L493" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">parabolic_general_sol := u(t, x) = int(A(k)*U(t, x, k), k = a..b);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L496" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">In the above, <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiQUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRImtGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiQUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRImtGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==</Equation> is an arbitrary function. Plugging <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> into the orginal PDE reveals that it is a genuine solution.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L482" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">gnat := dsubs(parabolic_general_sol, parabolic);
gnat := combine(dsubs(parabolic_sol, gnat));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVnbmF0R0YoLyIiIUYvNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L487" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Alternatively, we can use the pdetest command to check that <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">parabolic_general_sol</Font> solves the parabolic PDE:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L502" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">pdetest(subs(parabolic_sol, parabolic_general_sol), parabolic);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L501" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The moral of the story is that <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">pdsolve</Font> by itself does not always return the general solution of a differential equation unlike <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">dsolve</Font>. Also, one quickly discovers that it fails to return solutions for many different PDEs of interest. This reflects the basic truth that PDEs are harder to solve than ODEs.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Numerically solving PDEs using <Font size="18" style="Maple Input" executable="false">pdsolve</Font><Font size="18" style="Text">/</Font><Font size="18" style="Maple Input" executable="false">numeric</Font></Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L486" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Let us now turn our attention to the following wave equation.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L492" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">V := 'V':
pde := diff(phi(t, x), t, t)-diff(phi(t, x), x, x)+V(x)*phi(t, x);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRwZGVHRigsKC1JJWRpZmZHRiY2JC1JJHBoaUdGKDYkSSJ0R0YoSSJ4R0YoLUkiJEdGJjYkRjUiIiMiIiItRjA2JEYyLUY4NiRGNkY6ISIiKiYtSSJWR0YoNiNGNkY7RjJGO0Y7NyMsKC1GMDYkLUYwNiRGMkY1RjVGOy1GMDYkLUYwNiRGMkY2RjZGQEZBRjs=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L488" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Here, <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiVkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiVkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy1JKG1mZW5jZWRHRiQ2JC1GIzYkLUYsNiVRInhGJ0YvRjIvRjNRJ25vcm1hbEYnRj1GPQ==</Equation> is a potential function. We choose a potential as follows.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L483" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">x0 := 100;
V := x -&gt; exp(-(x-x0/3)^2)+exp(-(x+x0/3)^2);
p1 := plot(V(x), x = -x0..x0, axes = boxed, color = blue):
p1;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSN4MEdGKCIkKyI3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJWR0YoZio2I0kieEdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoLCYtSSRleHBHRiU2IywkKiQsJjkkIiIiSSN4MEdGKCMhIiIiIiQiIiNGP0Y8LUY2NiMsJCokLCZGO0Y8Rj0jRjxGQEZBRj9GPEYoRihGKDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="Maple Plot" layout="Maple Plot"><Plot height="500.0" originalheight="500.0" type="two-dimensional" width="500.0" originalwidth="500.0" plot-scale="1.0" plot-xtrans="0.0" plot-ytrans="0.0" gridlinevisibility="1" legendvisibility="false" input="_ATTRIBUTE(&quot;input&quot; = [TABLE([1 = plot, 2 = [exp(-(x-100/3)^2)+exp(-(x+100/3)^2)], 3 = (x = -100 .. 100), 4 = (axes = boxed), 5 = (color = blue)]), &quot;originalview&quot; = [-99.5000000000000000 .. 99.5000000000000000, 0. .. .972604475999999996], &quot;originalaxesticks&quot; = AXESTICKS(DEFAULT, DEFAULT, _ATTRIBUTE(&quot;source&quot; = &quot;mathdefault&quot;))])"></Plot></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L467" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">In this case, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">pdsolve</Font> can succeed in separating variables but cannot integrate the resulting set of ODEs.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L474" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">build(pdsolve(pde));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L489" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">So, we instead look for a numeric solution. To do so, we need to choose initial and boundary conditions for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, which we arrange in a list called <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">IBC</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L500" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">f := x -&gt; exp(-(x-x0/2)^2/16);
IBC := [phi(0, x) = f(x), D[1](phi)(0, x) = D(f)(x), phi(t, -2*x0) = 0, phi(t, 2*x0) = 0];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJmR0YoZio2I0kieEdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoLUkkZXhwR0YlNiMsJCokLCY5JCIiIkkjeDBHRigjISIiIiIjRj8jRj4iIztGKEYoRig3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRJQkNHRig3Ji8tSSRwaGlHRig2JCIiIUkieEdGKC1JJGV4cEdGJTYjLCQqJCwmRjQiIiIhI11GOyIiIyMhIiIiIzsvLS0mSSJER0YlNiNGOzYjRjFGMiomLCZGNCNGPyIiKSMiI0QiIiVGO0Y7RjVGOy8tRjE2JEkidEdGKCEkKyNGMy8tRjE2JEZSIiQrI0YzNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L464" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The numeric solution is obtained by calling <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">pdsolve</Font> with the option <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">numeric</Font>. Note that the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">timestep</Font> and <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">spacestep</Font> command are optional.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L465" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">pde_sol := pdsolve(pde, IBC, numeric, timestep = 1/4, spacestep = 1/2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L480" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">We can generate a movie of the solution by calling the following.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L472" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">movie := pde_sol:-animate(t = 0..250, axes = boxed, frames = 50):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L470" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Notice in the above that instead of displaying the movie, we have assigned it to a variable. We can get Maple to diplay the actual movie by just calling <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">movie</Font> (click on it to play).</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L468" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">movie;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="Maple Plot" layout="Maple Plot"><Plot height="500.0" originalheight="500.0" type="two-dimensional" width="500.0" originalwidth="500.0" plot-scale="1.0" plot-xtrans="0.0" plot-ytrans="0.0" gridlinevisibility="1" legendvisibility="false" input=""></Plot></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L494" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">We can also superimpose the potential on the movie by using display.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L497" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">display([movie, p1]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="Maple Plot" layout="Maple Plot"><Plot height="500.0" originalheight="500.0" type="two-dimensional" width="500.0" originalwidth="500.0" plot-scale="1.0" plot-xtrans="0.0" plot-ytrans="0.0" gridlinevisibility="1" legendvisibility="false" input=""></Plot></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L471" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">There are a variety of other ways to interact with <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">pdsolve</Font><Font style="Text">/</Font><Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">numeric</Font>. For example, the following generates a 3D plot of <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> over a given range in <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEidEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEidEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L478" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">p2 := pde_sol:-plot3d(t = 0..200, x = -x0..x0, grid = [100, 100], style = patchnogrid, axes = boxed, shading = ZHUE):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L481" drawlabel="true">
